for a,b in repls.items():s=s.replace(a,b)
# Add authoritative correction strip and feasibility matrix, plus held option.
pos=s.index('<section id="premise">')
s=s[:pos]+'''<section class="callout"><div class="eyebrow">CAPTAIN CORRECTIONS · SEPTEMBER 30</div><p><b>Sacrifices happen during the game. A blind player ends the game still blind. Removed players leave the game.</b> This draft gets harder by shrinking from four to one; no need for everyone to see the ending.</p><p>Saturday October 31 · lower-floor finished space + basement · about five groups of four · 15–30 minute runs · XY board is a from-scratch build; preserve the laser cutter.</p></section>'''+s[pos:]
pos=s.index('<section id="ouija">')
s=s[:pos]+'''<section class="panel"><div class="eyebrow">SHRINKING-TEAM CHECK</div><h2>Every remaining player still has a job.</h2><div class="grid2"><p><b>4 players / sight:</b> three can see; the blind witness aligns a tactile edge, holds the map or listens. Choose one sighted guest for sacrifice.</p><p><b>3 players / hearing:</b> blind witness can lead the listening; two sighted teammates manipulate clues. Remove one sighted guest.</p><p><b>2 players / touch:</b> blind witness feels and selects; the sighted partner reads, positions and guides. Seat the witness, then remove the partner.</p><p><b>1 blind player / speech + Ouija:</b> raised-dot sequencing, spoken instructions, audible board letters and tactile offering ring. No reading, color matching or second pair of hands required.</p></div><p><b>HELD OPTION — sacrificed guests become children who oppose the survivors.</b> Captain likes the idea but worries about novice complexity. Default: they exit. Optional later test: one simple scripted knock or misleading line, with a dedicated briefing; do not add free-form sabotage or secretly assume a third operator.</p></section>'''+s[pos:]
# Remove dangling choice wording already resolved; keep as production tuning rather than reopening core decisions.
